    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #304\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-274-review-debt-09-12-correct-the-idle-fol-thr_5b3q84ii9r` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes the three post-merge review findings from issue #196 raised in issue #274:\n\n1. **`imapIdleLifecycle.ts`** — Corrected `ImapIdleTransport.resolveFolders`'s doc comment: it now states the actual behavior (called once per `start()`, resolved paths held for the lifecycle's lifetime, folder rename/addition picked up only on next restart) instead of the incorrect claim about re-resolving on reconnect. `runFolderLoop`'s behavior was left untouched, as scoped.\n\n2. **`imapIdleClient.ts`** — `ImapFlowIdleConnection` now receives a `detachSignalListeners` callback built at `connect()` registration time. `close()` calls it before `closeQuietly`/`logout`, removing exactly the `exists`/`expunge`/`flags` listeners so no signal can reach `onSignal` after `close()` resolves. The existing `error`/`close` cleanup in `endPromiseFor` is untouched, and `removeAllListeners()` was deliberately avoided.\n\n3. **`imapIdleLifecycle.test.ts`** — Removed the unused `chokePoint` variable, its `beforeEach` assignment, the `createChokePoint` import, and the now-unused `ChokePoint` type import.\n\nAdded a regression test in `imapIdleClient.test.ts`: `FakeImapFlow` gained an `emitOnLogout` hook to simulate a final server push (e.g. `exists`) during logout/BYE, and a new test asserts `onSignal` is never invoked once `close()` has resolved (fails without the listener-removal fix).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm -r run build` in `backend/` succeeds.\n- `pnpm test` (full backend suite) passes: 24 test files, 314 tests, all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
